     ssccrreeeenn..lluuaa — bootloader screen manipulation module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssccrreeeenn..lluuaa contains functionality for manipulating the screen.  This in‐
     cludes functionality such as clearing the screen, moving the cursor, and
     setting foreground/background colors using sequences provided by
     color.lua(8).

     Before using the functionality provided by ssccrreeeenn..lluuaa, it must be in‐
     cluded with a statement such as the following:

           local screen = require("screen")

     The following variables are exported from ssccrreeeenn..lluuaa:

           ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffaauulltt__xx     The x component of the default cursor posi‐
                                tion.

           ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffaauulltt__yy     The y component of the default cursor posi‐
                                tion.

     The following functions are exported from ssccrreeeenn..lluuaa:

           ssccrreeeenn..cclleeaarr()   Clears the screen.  ssccrreeeenn..cclleeaarr() will do nothing
                            if a serial boot is detected.

           ssccrreeeenn..sseettccuurrssoorr(_x, _y)
                            Sets the cursor position to _x, _y.
                            ssccrreeeenn..sseettccuurrssoorr() will do nothing if a serial
                            boot is detected.

           ssccrreeeenn..sseettffoorreeggrroouunndd(_c_o_l_o_r___v_a_l_u_e)
                            Sets the foreground color to _c_o_l_o_r___v_a_l_u_e, which
                            should be a constant defined in color.lua(8).
                            ssccrreeeenn..sseettffoorreeggrroouunndd() will do nothing if color is
                            disabled.

           ssccrreeeenn..sseettbbaacckkggrroouunndd(_c_o_l_o_r___v_a_l_u_e)
                            Sets the background color to _c_o_l_o_r___v_a_l_u_e, which
                            should be a constant defined in color.lua(8).
                            ssccrreeeenn..sseettbbaacckkggrroouunndd() will do nothing if color is
                            disabled.

           ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffccoolloorr()
                            Sets the default color scheme, as defined by
                            ccoolloorr..ddeeffaauulltt().  ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffccoolloorr() will do noth‐
                            ing if color is disabled.

           ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffccuurrssoorr()
                            Sets the default cursor position to that defined
                            by ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffaauulltt__xx, ssccrreeeenn..ddeeffaauulltt__yy.

